  "about": {
    "missionBadge": "About the Mission",
    "headline": "Engineering a clearer future.",
    "description": "Oiyo Blog is a knowledge academy that unpacks psychology, fortune, money, science, and everyday life with well-sourced material — a place to understand your test results, build practical skills, and see the world one layer deeper.",
    "philosophyHeading": "The Philosophy",
    "philosophyText": "We value evidence over verdicts. Psychology content names its academic scales and limits, money and tax guides are checked against official sources, and mystic topics are treated as a language for self-observation, not destiny.",
    "whatWeCoverHeading": "What we cover",
    "coverItem1Title": "Self-understanding & psychology:",
    "coverItem1Text": "Scale-based explainers for MBTI, Big Five, attachment styles, and more.",
    "coverItem2Title": "Money & everyday skills:",
    "coverItem2Text": "Ready-to-use checklists and guides for tax, finance, moving, and travel.",
    "coverItem3Title": "Knowledge & mystic:",
    "coverItem3Text": "From science primers to saju, tarot, and astrology — reading in depth.",
    "quote": "The best way to predict the future is to engineer it.",
    "connectHeading": "Connect with the Team",
    "teamHeading": "Who writes this — our editorial desks",
    "teamIntro": "OIYO content is not written by an anonymous individual but by topic-specific editorial desks that verify against primary sources and public statistics. Each desk's remit:",
    "methodHeading": "How we work — editorial principles",
    "methodText": "Every piece (1) checks facts against primary sources, official statistics, and academic literature; (2) states limits and disclaimers for sensitive topics like psychology and health; and (3) carries an updated date and is revised on a regular cycle when the topic changes. Our goal is to give you a basis to judge for yourself rather than a verdict."
